            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Angela W"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I think this recipe has great potential.. While I am not a big fan of \"baked\" pork chop recipes, I think this one is excellent under the broiler. I just personally think that broiling is more flavorful than baking. The lemon juice accents the barbecue sauce with just enough \"zing\" and adds great flavor. I highly recommend people to try this, but with broiling 4-5 mins on each side instead of baking it in the sauce."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Tammy Lynn"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I needed something simple and quick, and this fit the bill. I used Sweet Baby Ray's, and the lemon tang was nice with the sweet sauce. I sauted some minced garlic in a little canola oil first and then sprinkled the chops with lemon pepper before putting them in the BBQ sauce and then into the pan. My chops were a little thin, so they were done in about 15 min. I'll use this method again if I need something simple and quick. ;) I served with butternut squash and green beans. It made a nice meal.",
            "datePublished": "2013-10-09T10:40:26.647Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "NJSS2000"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I added seasonings like garlic, pepper, salt, etc. I also did in the crock pot and my husband was full of compliments. So easy and definitely a do again recipe.",
            "datePublished": "2014-03-30T04:44:40.430Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "sask"
            },
            "reviewBody": "ADD LEMON ZEST FOR MORE \"ZING\"\nCooked this for kids -- they LOVED it. I cooked in electric skillet, used KC Masterpiece sauce, and sprinkled the zest from two lemons on chops while cooking (in addition to the lemon juice).",
            "datePublished": "2007-09-25T09:17:54.813Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "mmcoble"
            },
            "reviewBody": "A solid recipe. Quick, easy, and very inexpensive! My recommendation would be to marinate the pork chops for at least an hour in order to get more of a barbecue flavor.",
            "datePublished": "2011-01-30T17:10:16.187Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "kat3260"
            },
            "reviewBody": "If you're running low on time &amp; money, this is a great quick fix recipe. I used Stubb's barbeque sauce &amp; juiced 2 fresh lemons (they were small). Only took 20 minutes on the stovetop. Served w/ rice pilaf &amp; a salad...everyone enjoyed!",
            "datePublished": "2007-01-18T10:02:29.543Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "TAEMARIE"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was a decent recipe, great for those in a bind however. I used plain BBQ sauce, but I think if I'd used a spicey or bold it would have tasted much better. I'll make this again though, will just switch sauces!",
            "datePublished": "2005-06-13T11:29:03.500Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "NMChef1"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I'm mixed about what rating to give the recipe. It was pretty tasty, but also a very simple recipe. I made it exactly as written, using boneless top loin pork chops, and I can't say that the lemon juice was noticeable in the end. The 2 cups of barbecue sauce was overkill, too; I love barbecue sauce, but 1 cup or maybe a little more would have been enough, I think. Still, I enjoyed eating this as is, served with rice that could soak up some extra sauce.",
            "datePublished": "2013-04-14T18:25:02.727Z"
          },
